{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1189,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When Galileo pointed his telescope at Jupiter\nin 1610, he was the first person to see the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6110,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giant orbs attached to it by springs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9170,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His actual drawings, compared night after\nnight, show these bright spots moving back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12950,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and forth past Jupiter, exactly the same as\nif they were balls hanging off of springs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17790,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, yeah Galileo was looking at the moons\nof Jupiter, but if you plot their motion back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22380,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and forth and back and forth over time, it\nforms a sine wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26000,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that motion is mathematically identical\nto the motion of something bouncing up and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30030,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down on a spring with a linear restoring force\n- also sine waves over time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34620,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a side-on perspective that projects two\ndimensions down to one, things in circular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38760,
    "dDurationMs": 4819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbits look exactly like they’re springing\nback and forth on giant coils of wire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43579,
    "dDurationMs": 3761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I’m not saying that we should think\nof the moons of Jupiter as being held on by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47340,
    "dDurationMs": 3999,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giant invisible springs, but it’s a valid\nmathematical model when viewing them from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51339,
    "dDurationMs": 4671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a distance – it’ll make the same predictions\nabout the motions of the moons as the “orbiting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56010,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in circles due to invisible gravity” model,\nand one can be mathematically transformed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60190,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The moons of Jupiter aren’t alone in having\nmultiple mathematical descriptions: projectiles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65840,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and storms on earth experience a force (called\nthe Coriolis effect) that causes them to turn,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71180,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but viewed from an external perspective, the\nprojectiles and storms are what goes in a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74410,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "straight line while the earth turns beneath\nthem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76970,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both models, if you use them carefully, make\ncorrect predictions about reality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81690,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And quantum phenomena can be modeled in at\nleast three different ways that all give the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85710,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same predictions: as a particle being guided\nby a spread-out “pilot wave”, or as a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90530,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spread out probability wave that collapses\nto a single point, or as a particle exploring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94600,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all possible paths it could take and interfering\nwith itself along the way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98740,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All three of these mathematical models suggest\ndifferent ways of thinking about what’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102950,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“actually” going on in quantum mechanics,\nand the fact that all of them give the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106870,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experimental predictions suggests that perhaps\nnone of them is the “right” way to picture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111070,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what’s happening in quantum systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112450,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mathematical models give us nice, easy-to-digest\npictures of how the universe works: moons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117070,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbit around planets, atoms bind together\ninto molecules, electrons are clouds of probability,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121630,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122880,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we need to be careful how much weight\nwe give to the models in our heads (or on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126670,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our blackboards, or computer screens)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128420,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do Jupiter’s moons move like they’re pulled\nback and forth by the invisible force of springs?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133640,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or held in orbits by the invisible force of\ngravity?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136240,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or are they following helical paths which\nare actually straight lines in curved spacetime?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141310,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way we describe the world influences the\nway we think the world is, even when there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146150,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are other, equally correct ways of describing\nthe world that paint entirely different pictures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150810,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151810,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s not to say we should accept wrong\nideas, but we should be aware that sometimes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156100,
    "dDurationMs": 6090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a different correct picture, one we haven’t\nconsidered, is the one we need to see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162190,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, Henry here, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165150,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video has been supported by Audible.com,\nas you may know, a leading provider of audiobooks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including fiction, non-fiction and periodicals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172480,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can get a free 30-day trial at audible.com/minutephysics,\nand I’d like to recommend the book “The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177290,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Power of Habit” by Charles Duhigg, which\nexplores how we form habits, how to break"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181810,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them, and how to use them to your advantage\n– it’s a good one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184090,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can listen to “The Power of Habit”\nor another book of your choice, with a free"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187170,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "30-day trial at Audible.com/minutephysics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190460,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks again for watching, and thanks to audible\nfor supporting these videos."
    } ]
  } ]
}
